{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_quyie5q2wtl4xoq2qdkzl5rkzgiku5lvawrpay65gdap7zdra4ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass. **The Rust translation is correct; `src/lib.rs` needed no changes.**\n\n## What the library is\n\nA single 14-line C function, `unsigned hdr_bitrate(const uint8_t *h)` — an MPEG-audio-header bitrate lookup. Branch-free: one `return` indexing `static const uint8_t halfrate[2][3][15]`.\n\n## Results against the completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | 1 symbol in C, 1 in Rust, diff **empty**; 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | 16/16 rows pass, 17 tests |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | 10/10 rows pass, 11 tests |\n| Every feature combination | `[features]` is **absent** ⇒ exactly one combination; verified in debug **and** release |\n\nCoverage is **exhaustive, not sampled**: the function reads only `h[1]` and `h[2]`, so all 256×256 = 65536 distinguishable inputs are tested byte-for-byte. There is no well-defined input that can separate the two implementations.\n\n## Two findings worth flagging\n\n**1. The test suite was initially vacuous — I caught it with mutation testing.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib` (integration tests don't link it), so my harness loaded a **stale** `.so`. It reported 28 green tests while **all 9 deliberate mutations survived**. `ensure_rust_so()` now runs `cargo build --lib` into a separate `--target-dir` (distinct build lock, no deadlock) and asserts the artifact is newer than `src/lib.rs`. After the fix: **12 of 13 mutants killed**; the survivor (`PAD 15→16`) is a *provably equivalent* mutant, since `PAD` appears in both the write and read offsets. Notably, the two \"naive fixes\" a translator would be tempted to apply — clamping negative `j` to 0, clamping `k` to 14 — are both killed.\n\n**2. The C has genuine UB, and the Rust reproduces it without itself being UB.** `j = ((h[1]>>1)&3) - 1` can be `-1` and `k = h[2]>>4` can be `15`, so the C reads outside its 90-byte table for 8192 of the 65536 inputs. Because C array indexing is flat, most of those still land *inside* the table on a neighbouring row (e.g. `i=1, j=-1` silently aliases `halfrate[0][2]`) — I verified the Rust preserves that aliasing rather than \"fixing\" it. Only two families truly escape the object, and both observe `0`. Rather than assume that, I measured it: the full suite passes against **eight** independently built C `.so`s (cmake default, `gcc -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`, `clang -O0/-O2`) via a new `HDR_C_SO` override. It is still formally UB, and `ERRORS.md` records that a toolchain placing non-zero bytes adjacent to the table would diverge — a property of the C, not a defect in the translation.\n\nAlso confirmed: `err_e7` shows C and Rust both die with **SIGSEGV (11)** on a null pointer (run in child processes), and `c_src/` is untouched — original mtimes and md5sums intact.\n\nDeliverables: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{harness/mod.rs,differential.rs,errors.rs}`, and `scripts/{verify_all,check_all_features,run_all_features,symbol_parity}.sh`. `bash scripts/verify_all.sh` reproduces the entire gate end to end."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":90188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af1479d7-476a-4e7a-8868-3ff4e5d8c7aa","uuid":"2ea25f0d-7174-47d6-a3d8-643373634886","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:34:33.707Z"}
